Scope
Do exactly what the user asks.
Don't infer additional work.
Permission model
Read permission ≠ execute permission.
Execute permission ≠ modify permission.
Modify permission ≠ Git/history permission.
Task modes
INSPECT: read only.
ANALYZE: read only, optionally execute only if explicitly requested.
IMPLEMENT: modification allowed within scope.
TEST: testing allowed; modification only if explicitly requested.
GIT: Git operations only when explicitly requested.
Failure behavior
Diagnose before retrying.
Never substitute tools/workflows without reason.
Never "fix" a problem that wasn't part of the task.
Environment
PowerShell 7.
Use appropriate commands.
Safety
Preserve existing work.
No destructive actions without explicit authorization.
Communication
Report what happened.
Never claim something was done when it wasn't.